i know dyson offers says the say at leon  st is more stylish than vw's golf  variant and sportier than skoda's  octavia combi  the experienced variant of the leon st  offers three centimeters more clearance  all-wheel drive and plastic under body  cladding  now he's going to see what it can do on  the street and light terrain  the new leon experience is seatt's way  of saying  it doesn't always have to be an suv its  off-road appearance  also looks at home on city streets from  a technical standpoint  it has a lot in common with the vw golf  but in comparison with the gulf the leon  is sportier and appeals to the emotions  the additional clearance has taken  nothing away from its dynamic  handling on curves  the experience is a special model leon  which boasts top  quality equipment the body is beefed up  with molding for a more rugged look  while inside it features all-wheel drive  connected to a haldex clutch  once the experience leaves the smooth  asphalt it puts in a decent showing  off-road  experience einhold believes the word  experience connotes adventure and says  adventures are better talked about than  personally had  the leon experience will most often be  used for runs to school  or work and maybe for an occasional trip  into the mountains  and if the chalet lies a bit far off the  beaten track the experience can handle  steep inclines surprisingly well  order  the additional clearance is very welcome  on rough terrain  gravel roads and slopes the experience  can even edge down  steep hills without giving the driver  panic attacks  we tested the strongest diesel engine  with 135 kilowatts and a 6p  dsg transmission it accelerates from  zero to 100 kilometers per hour  in a decent 7.1 seconds and reaches a  top speed of 224 kilometers per hour  it consumes just 4.9 liters of fuel per  100 kilometers  the suspension ensures a comfortable  ride even over  uneven ground  reinhold confirms that it feels steady  yet when he takes the curves with a bit  more speed  the front axle feels somehow different  he cites two reasons  one the all-wheel drive allocates the  power between the rear and front axles  according to need two the experience has  a differential lock  that strives to keep the varying speeds  on the front right and left wheels in  sync  it provides a feeling of better grip  that's especially nice on wet pavement  snow and ice  from the outside the additional  clearance is immediately apparent  the wheel arches are framed by black  plastic cladding  which gives the design more of a  practical off-road look  the black plastic skirting contrasts  with the painted surfaces at the rear as  well  the cargo space is a respectable 587  liters which more than doubles to 1  470 liters with the easy back release  rear seats down  the folding mid gate is practical for  carrying long objects  like skis the experience logo  graces the steering wheel and orange  stitching sets a colorful accent  the dashboard controls make for a tidy  impression  and the multimedia unit is accessible  over a 5.8 inch screen  in the center console the seats provide  good lateral support for a comfortable  ride  in germany the normal station wagon with  the strongest diesel engine starts at  just over 30  000 euros if you want the all-wheel  drive version you'll need to buy the  experience which cost  two thousand seven hundred fifty euros  more the experience  reinhold points out that the experience  is a bit pricier than the sea  leon without the x but for that you get  an outdoor vehicle with a stylish  appearance  and this is one of seatt's main  advantages over its competitors  who all too often flood their wares with  the charm of a used car salesman
 

